// Compile-time benchmark input: imports every std module, so with VELT_EAGER_STD=1 sema checks
// all of std and the prelude (without it, the prelude's free functions and statics this program
// doesn't reach stay unchecked; docs/internals/design/lazy-std.md). bench/nightly.sh divides its
// instructions with VELT_EAGER_STD=1 by the code lines of all of std/, which is only a cost per
// line when all of std is checked; crates/veltc/tests/bench_programs.rs checks that no module is
// missing and that all of std checks without diagnostics. A small main touches a few modules and names the globals
// loaded on demand whose modules nothing imports (`Proxy` and `Reflect`,
// std/prelude/global/proxy.vlt).
